# Raw media and generated data are big/binary — keep them out of git.
# The clip LOG (clips.csv) and labels ARE tracked (small, text, valuable).
#
# We ignore the CONTENTS of these dirs but keep the dirs themselves (via the
# .gitkeep files) so the pipeline always has somewhere to write. Note: you
# cannot un-ignore a file inside a fully-ignored directory, so we ignore
# contents with `dir/*` and then re-include the .gitkeep.

raw_clips/*
!raw_clips/.gitkeep

frames/*
!frames/.gitkeep

dataset/*
!dataset/.gitkeep
